From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 02:53:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 87/87] web-app: Telegram-style reply threads as a message list
 mode

A message that has replies shows a reply-arrow badge with the number of
all replies below it (nested ones included) before its timestamp.
Clicking the badge switches the message list into thread mode: it shows
only that reply thread (its root plus every reply below it, any depth
and branching), scrolled to and highlighting the message you came from.

Thread mode is the real message list, not a separate view: the message
list store takes an optional thread, and its five item loads go through
one helper (fetchMessageListItems) that returns the thread's messages
instead of the chat's. Paging, jumps, live updates on the chat's events,
reactions, multiselect, keyboard navigation and the composer with its
draft all work unchanged; on small screens the mode is full-screen
because the message list is. After the first load the thread is
anchored on its root, so deleting the message you entered from doesn't
end it; if the thread can't be loaded at all, the view drops back to
the chat.

- Header: in thread mode the navbar shows the chat's avatar and name over
  the first line of the thread's first message, a toggle between the
  chronological list and a tree layout, and a button back to the chat
  (which also replaces the small-screen back arrow).
- Tree layout: replies sit below the message they answer, siblings stay
  chronological, each indented by its depth (capped at 4) with a guide
  line. Order and depth come from layoutThread(), tested in
  replyThreadLayout.test.ts.
- Composer: in thread mode a message only stays in the thread if it
  quotes one of the thread's messages, so sending (and stickers) wait for
  such a quote; a bar in the quote slot says so and offers "Reply to
  latest". The draft is the chat's draft.
- Leaving: jumping to a message outside the thread (a quote, a search
  result) leaves thread mode first; "Show in chat" in a bubble's context
  menu leaves it and lands on that message; switching chats resets it.
  Badges are hidden in thread mode.
- Badge counts are fetched in one batch per visible page
  (getMessageReplyCounts), again (throttled) on the chat's events,
  instead of one request per bubble per event. The badge itself is
  presentational.
- The badge's `button-reset` now comes before the shared metadata rule,
  so it gets the metadata font size and color, and it is in the
  per-direction color rules (outgoing, sticker) like the date.

The published @deltachat/jsonrpc-client pin predates the new methods, so
they're widened locally in backend/replyThreads.ts, same pattern as
useMessage's MessageData. Icons are Google Material Symbols (reply,
account_tree, view_list). New i18n keys: reply_thread, n_replies
(plural), thread_reply_needs_quote, thread_reply_to_latest,
thread_show_as_tree, thread_show_as_list, thread_close.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
